# Copy to .env and adjust.  .env is gitignored — never commit real values.
#   cp .env.example .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Host port mappings
# NOTE: this machine already runs a local PostgreSQL on 5432 and a
# local MySQL on 3306/33060. We deliberately publish on alternate
# host ports so the containers never collide with them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
AIRFLOW_UI_PORT=8080
MYSQL_HOST_PORT=3307        # -> container 3306  (staging)
POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5433     # -> container 5432  (analytics)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging database (MySQL) — raw landing + cleaned staging
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
MYSQL_DATABASE=flight_staging
MYSQL_USER=flight
MYSQL_PASSWORD=change_me_staging
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=change_me_root

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics database (PostgreSQL) — facts + KPI marts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_DB=flight_analytics
POSTGRES_USER=flight
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change_me_analytics

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Airflow
# AIRFLOW_UID must match your host uid or the container writes
# root-owned files into ./logs and ./dags. Find it with: id -u
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
AIRFLOW_UID=1000

# Secrets. docker-compose.yaml references both WITHOUT a default, so leaving
# them unset starts Airflow with an empty Fernet key and an empty JWT secret.
# `make init` generates real values; these placeholders exist so that a plain
# `cp .env.example .env` still produces a working stack rather than one that
# fails in a confusing way several containers later.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   FERNET_KEY:  openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_'
#   JWT secret:  openssl rand -hex 32
FERNET_KEY=REPLACE_ME_generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32_tr_urlsafe=
AIRFLOW__API_AUTH__JWT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME_generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32
AIRFLOW_ADMIN_USER=airflow
AIRFLOW_ADMIN_PASSWORD=airflow

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pipeline behaviour
#
# This file holds SECRETS and HOST-SPECIFIC settings only. Pipeline tunables
# — thresholds, batch size, the fare markup factor, the validation regexes —
# live in include/config/pipeline.yml, with the reasoning beside each value.
#
# These three previously appeared here as well, duplicating both the values
# and their explanations. Two files describing one setting is how they end up
# disagreeing, and how a reader learns to trust neither.
#
# They remain supported as environment overrides for a one-off run, but are
# left unset so pipeline.yml is the single source of truth:
#
#   SOURCE_CSV_PATH=/opt/airflow/include/data/raw/some_other_extract.csv
#   REJECT_RATE_THRESHOLD=0.10
#   FARE_TOLERANCE_BDT=0.01
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
